# EWS UNIVERSAL RIG & NODE MAPPING GUIDE (EWS-MAP/1)
*The Rosetta Stone for 3D Modeling, Modding, Story Visuals, and AI Verification*

---

## 1. PURPOSE & WHY THIS PREVENTS ENGINE COLLAPSE
When modeling, creating mods, or scripting story sequences in the visual editor, nodes will naturally be nudged, added, or renamed. Without a semantic mapping guide, hardcoded scripts break whenever a node name changes.

This mapping guide provides a **semantic layer of abstraction**:
- Story editors, clothing mods, and combat hitboxes reference **Sockets** and **Roles** (e.g., `socket_hat` or `role_head`), never volatile raw indices.
- If Dylan adds an extra neck joint or renames `head` to `skull_main`, the mapping guide updates the target node mapping, and **all story scenes, clothing mods, and hair splines stay perfectly connected**.

---

## 2. ANATOMICAL SOCKETS & MOD ATTACHMENT MAP
| Socket Identifier | Primary Anchor | Purpose / Mod Attachment |
|---|---|---|
| `socket_hat` | `head` | Helmets, caps, goggles, eyewear |
| `socket_horn` | `head` | Unicorn magic horns, head armor plating |
| `socket_crest_mane` | `head -> chest` | Nape/crest hair spline ribbons |
| `socket_forelock` | `head` | Brow bangs and forehead tufts |
| `socket_tail` | `pelvis` | Tail plumes, ribbons, armor guards |
| `socket_saddle` | `chest` | Saddles, packs, harnesses, barding |
| `socket_left_wing` | `chest` | Pegasus left wing armature |
| `socket_right_wing` | `chest` | Pegasus right wing armature |
| `socket_hoof_FL/FR` | `FL4 / FR4` | Horseshoes, combat wraps, boots |
| `socket_hoof_BL/BR` | `BL4 / BR4` | Hind horseshoes, caltrops, armor |
| `socket_organ_bag` | `chest + rear` | Centroid boundary for all internal viscera |

